  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper reviews two decades of academic literature examining how air transport directly, indirectly, and through spillover effects impacts the economic, environmental, and social development of cities and regions. The analysis maps how these different types of impacts are distributed across the three pillars of sustainability and identifies which moderating factors influence these relationships.",
      "why": "It synthesizes a fragmented body of research to reveal that scientific attention is unevenly distributed, showing where empirical evidence is robust and where critical gaps remain regarding the combined and spillover effects of aviation on regional development."
    }
  },
